# Layout

## Width strategy

Content is **fluid at 100%** of the main region width, with **constant lateral
gutters only** (`--space-16` on the main padding). No centered max-width column.

- Operational surfaces (Overview, Match, Calendrier, Classements): fill the main
  area edge-to-gutter.
- Forms / focused tasks / dialogs: constrained width (28–40rem), never full width.
- Text never touches the viewport edge — gutters handle that, not a narrow column.

## Asymmetric composition ("asymétrie signifiante")

- The dominant region must visibly weigh more: hero band ≈ 1.6/1,
  two-column groups ≈ 1.45/1 (`dlab-grid-2--major`), never mechanical 50/50
  unless the two blocks are true peers.
- The reading order is: situation (top-left, largest) → next action (top-right)
  → pending work → detail.

## Density

- Standard density everywhere; grids may be denser but rows stay ≥ 40px tall.
- Whitespace between groups > whitespace inside groups.

## Responsive

- Two-column groups collapse to one column below 56rem, dominant block first.
- The Match Hero stacks: status → teams+score → meta.
- Accueil (hors Shell): same chrome breakpoints as the shell (phone
  `<48rem`, tablet `<64rem`). Lockup is one composition (mark + wordmark +
  tagline) and **scales as a unit** in the 42rem column — no reflow, no wrap.
